WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:09.024
Job three: make things better. Why it matters: Vanderbilt is asking every team to move faster and improve,

2
00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:16.049
and that does not happen from the top. It happens in your team, in small ways, every week.

3
00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:19.952
Four habits, and none of them is a reorganization.

4
00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:24.089
Explain the why: a new system is coming from central;

5
00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:31.660
tell your team the reason in your own words at Thursday’s meeting, before Tuesday’s campus email,

6
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.173
and write down their objections to take back.

7
00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:38.841
Describe where you are going: in two sentences,

8
00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:43.993
what your team will be able to do next year that it cannot do now.

9
00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:52.345
Let people try: someone suggests a new way to run the weekly report; say, try it for two weeks and show me.

10
00:00:52.395 --> 00:00:59.526
Look back: ten minutes after any big piece of work, what worked, what did not, what changes,

11
00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:02.805
written where the next person can find it.

12
00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:09.830
What to stop doing: forwarding the announcement, and saying that is not how we do it here.

13
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.030
This week: hold one ten-minute look-back.

14
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:19.352
Now flip the cards on the page; your call on the new system comes after job four.

